    {
      "source_unit_key": "nn-in-the-loop.html::node-1203",
      "unit_text_sha256": "5cf21579be2b4a1c18c5dd67c511d548272e43493b5966342ae96de1ff3398f8",
      "source_sha256": "38da10308fe643801f74e751a43b2b168f88ca2a010803ecbf4d599777a9efeb",
      "source_text": "(b) $r(v)=\\tanh(v)/v$ ($r(0)=1$) is even, and for $v\\gt0$, $r'(v)=-h(v)/v^2$ with $h(v)=\\tanh v-v(1-\\tanh^2v)$. As $h(0)=0$ and $h'(v)=2v\\tanh v\\,(1-\\tanh^2v)\\gt0$, $h\\gt0$ and $r$ decreases strictly on $(0,\\infty)$. So $r(v)\\in[r(\\bar v),1)$ on $0\\lt|v|\\le\\bar v$, with the lower end attained at $\\pm\\bar v$ and the upper approached as $v\\to0$: the tightest sector is $[\\tanh(\\bar v)/\\bar v,1]$. $\\tanh'$ is even and decreasing in $|s|$, and a chord slope is the mean of $\\tanh'$ over a subinterval of $[-\\bar v,\\bar v]$, so it lies in $[1-\\tanh^2\\bar v,1]$; short chords near $\\pm\\bar v$ and near $0$ approach both ends.",
      "exercise_key": "nn-in-the-loop.html::exercise-16",
      "exercise_text_sha256": "4eff40e4da3e34630464c1fa8b57348828c45397934e51e0e05856851b2d5ce0",
